{
  "type": "agent",
  "provider": "hermes",
  "agent": "default",
  "thinking": "high",
  "timeout": 1800,
  "gateway_url": "127.0.0.1:9119",
  "bin": "hermes",
  "icon": "🪽",

  "_comment": [
    "Hermes as an external agent: it does its own thinking, keeps its own",
    "session memory and has its own tools, so LOS only hands it this agenda",
    "and a list of MCP tools.",
    "'bin' is the command LOS runs to reach Hermes. 'hermes' works when it is",
    "on $PATH; otherwise give the absolute path, for example",
    "/home/you/.local/bin/hermes.",
    "'agent' names the profile/session to use (the label in .config can",
    "override it with agent=<name>), and gateway_url is informational —",
    "'hermes serve' listens on 127.0.0.1:9119 by default.",
    "'thinking' is low, medium or high."
  ]
}
